---
title: "verify_webhook (Legion Backend Authentication)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_extract_sig: received_sig = headers["X-Signature"]
    q_extract_sig --> q_check_present: received_sig != null
    q_check_present --> q_compute: body = raw_request_body
    q_check_present --> q_reject: received_sig == null
    q_reject --> [*]: revert "missing signature header"
    q_compute --> q_hmac: expected_sig = HMAC_SHA256(secret_key, body)
    q_hmac --> q_compare: compare(expected_sig, received_sig)
    q_compare --> q_accept: expected_sig == received_sig
    q_compare --> q_deny: expected_sig != received_sig
    q_accept --> [*]: return authentic
    q_deny --> [*]: revert "signature mismatch"

    note right of q_compare
        INV-001: comparison must be constant-time to prevent timing attacks
        INV-002: webhook body must not be modified before signature recomputation
        INV-003: secret_key used for verification must match the key Legion used for signing
    end note
